// ======== foldSlot: a band of the surface folded into a wedge along a path ========
//
// An undercut groove with a crisp opening (the knight's mouth slit, an eyelid slit) laid on a surface that is
// otherwise a height field, as ONE surface: no boolean, no second mesh, no seam. The surface is built with the slot
// CLOSED (each cut runs straight across the mouth, so the opening is a flat chord); foldSlot then moves the opening's
// vertices into the wedge. This is how the 27 Nov 2026 front-strip experiment made the slit: the chord's vertices were
// moved into the triangle given by three tracks (roof end, apex, floor start) in the slit's cross-section plane.
//
// foldSlot(m, path, sections, width, maxEdge, maxPasses, problems):
//   - 'path' is the line of the wedge's APEX, as it falls on the surface: the apex lies under it. 'sections' are three
//     RunCurves in the run fraction t of the path's own length (0 at its first point, 1 at its last): the apex DEPTH,
//     the ROOF's angle and the FLOOR's angle, in radians, each wall's angle from the opening's plane at the opening
//     (an angle over a right angle is an undercut wall: it leans back over the groove). 'width' is the farthest from
//     the path, along the surface, that a wall's foot may be, and the band that is looked at; 'maxEdge' and
//     'maxPasses' are displaceRegion's.
//   - THE FRAME at a point of the path. 'n' is the base normal at the OPENING: the unit normals of the faces whose
//     centres lie near the opening's middle (found in two rounds, from a first guess, the vertex normals within
//     'width'). A 'path.up' that is not (0, 0, 0) is the first guess itself, at every point (made square
//     to T): give it where the opening is a small part of a curved band, where the vertex normals are not its own
//     normal (the knight's slit does, and the rounds fail from a poor guess), made square to the path's tangent T. INTO is -n, the direction of the depth. The SIDE is n x T. A
//     vertex's offset 'a' is its distance from the path along the side (the roof is on the positive side), its
//     place along the path the nearest point of the polyline; the frame between two points of the path is the blend of
//     theirs.
//   - THE WEDGE at run fraction t has its apex at 'depth' along INTO under the path (a = 0). The roof wall leaves the
//     apex up to the opening's plane at the roof's angle and meets it at a = depth / tan(roof) (its foot, on the roof's
//     side of the path; negative for an undercut wall); the floor wall at a = -depth / tan(floor). The OPENING is the
//     stretch of the plane between the two feet, floor foot to roof foot. Feet farther than 'width' from the path are held
//     to it, with a problem line.
//   - ASSIGNMENT AT THE APEX. The band, the opening, is split at its own middle: a vertex on the roof's side of it goes
//     to the roof wall, one on the other side to the floor wall, and each takes its place by arc length along its wall:
//     a vertex at fraction f of the way from the opening's edge to the middle goes to fraction f of the way from the
//     edge's foot to the apex. (Where the opening is centred on the path, as for a groove that is not undercut and is
//     symmetric, this is the path's own line.) The surface keeps its own curve and detail: the vertex moves by the
//     difference between where the wall puts it and where the plane had it, along the side and along INTO. A vertex at
//     or beyond a foot is not moved, so there is no step, and everything outside the opening is bit for bit the input.
//     The opening is the surface within half its own width of the opening's plane, along the normal: a part of the
//     surface that lies over or under it is not folded.
//   - ENDS. A wedge of zero depth has its feet at the path, the opening is nothing and the fold is the identity, so
//     it blends out smoothly wherever the depth falls toward 0. Make the depth 0 at the path's two ends: a vertex
//     beyond an end of the path (its nearest point is the end, across the end's plane) is not moved, so a depth above
//     0 at an end is a step.
//   - BENDS. Where the path bends so sharply that neighbouring cross-section planes (square to the path at
//     neighbouring points) meet within 'width' of the path, on the inside of the bend (the fanned muzzle cuts of the
//     design review): two neighbouring points a distance ds apart whose tangents turn by theta have planes that meet at
//     ds / theta from the path. On the inside the feet are held to that distance (the wall stays at its depth, so it is
//     steeper), and one problem line names the stations (the path's points) and the narrowest width used. If that is
//     below one edge length of the band's input (the mean of the edges that have an end in the opening) the call refuses.
//   - REFINEMENT is displaceRegion's, one driver (dsRun in heightpatch.cone): the region is the faces with a vertex in
//     the opening (not beyond the path's ends); every edge of it whose length AFTER the fold is over 'maxEdge' is split,
//     up to 'maxPasses' passes, the ring of faces beside split edges split to match, and a new vertex takes the fold at
//     its own place. Channels are carried as displaceRegion carries them.
//   - A REFUSAL is a problem line and an unchanged copy: a path of fewer than 2 points; 'width' or 'maxEdge' at or
//     below 0 (or not a number); sections not 3 curves; a depth below 0 or not a number; a wall's angle at or below 0
//     or at or over two right angles where the depth is above 0; walls that cross at positive depth (the floor's foot
//     beyond the roof's: the walls meet before the apex); a path point with no surface near it; a band limited below one
//     edge. No face in the opening is a silent copy.

struct SlotField {
  pts: List[Vec3];       // the path
  dist: List[f32];       // distance along the path to each point
  total: f32;
  tan: List[Vec3];       // per point: the unit tangent
  nrm: List[Vec3];       // per point: the base normal at the opening, unit and square to the tangent
  limPos: List[f32];     // per point: the farthest a foot on the positive side may be (width, or the bend's)
  limNeg: List[f32];     // per point: the same on the negative side
  tab: List[f32];        // depth, roof, floor, three to a sample, ts + 1 samples evenly in t
  ts: usize;
  width: f32;
}

struct SlotHit {
  k: usize;
  u: f32;
  q: Vec3;
  d2: f32;
  beyond: bool;          // the nearest point is an end of the path and the place is past it
}

// Where a place is against the wedge at its own station
struct SlotLocal {
  ok: bool;
  a: f32;                // its distance from the path along the side
  ar: f32;               // the roof foot
  af: f32;               // the floor foot
  depth: f32;
  down: Vec3;            // INTO, the direction of the depth
  side: Vec3;
}

fn slotNearest(f: &SlotField, p: Vec3) SlotHit {
  let n = f.pts.len();
  var best = SlotHit(0usize, 0., *f.pts[0usize], 3.0e38, false);
  var k = 0usize;
  while k + 1usize < n {
    let a = *f.pts[k];
    let seg = *f.pts[k + 1usize] - a;
    let l2 = seg.dot(seg);
    var raw: f32 = 0.;
    if l2 > 0. { raw = (p - a).dot(seg) / l2; }
    var u = raw;
    if u < 0. { u = 0.; }
    if u > 1. { u = 1.; }
    let q = a + seg * u;
    let d = p - q;
    let d2 = d.dot(d);
    if d2 < best.d2 {
      best = SlotHit(k, u, q, d2, (k == 0usize && raw < 0.) || (k + 2usize == n && raw > 1.));
    }
    k = k + 1usize;
  }
  best
}

fn slotTab(f: &SlotField, t: f32, c: usize) f32 {
  var x = t * f32.from(f.ts);
  if x < 0. { x = 0.; }
  var i = usize.from(libc.floorf(x));
  if i >= f.ts { i = f.ts - 1usize; }
  var fx = x - f32.from(i);
  if fx > 1. { fx = 1.; }
  *f.tab[3usize * i + c] * (1. - fx) + *f.tab[3usize * (i + 1usize) + c] * fx
}

// The roof's and floor's feet for depth d and the two angles, held to the limits lp (positive side) and ln (negative)
fn slotFoot(d: f32, ang: f32, sign: f32, lp: f32, ln: f32) f32 {
  var e = sign * d * ang.cos() / ang.sin();
  if e > lp { e = lp; }
  if e < -ln { e = -ln; }
  e
}

fn slotLocal(f: &SlotField, p: Vec3) SlotLocal {
  let none = SlotLocal(false, 0., 0., 0., 0., Vec3(0., 0., 0.), Vec3(0., 0., 0.));
  let h = slotNearest(f, p);
  if h.beyond { return none; }
  let k = h.k;
  let u = h.u;
  let tn = unit(*f.tan[k] * (1. - u) + *f.tan[k + 1usize] * u);
  var nn = *f.nrm[k] * (1. - u) + *f.nrm[k + 1usize] * u;
  nn = nn - tn * nn.dot(tn);
  if !(nn.dot(nn) > 0.) { return none; }
  nn = unit(nn);
  let side = unit(nn.cross(tn));
  let seg = (*f.pts[k + 1usize] - *f.pts[k]).length();
  var t: f32 = 0.;
  if f.total > 0. { t = (*f.dist[k] + u * seg) / f.total; }
  let depth = slotTab(f, t, 0usize);
  if !(depth > 0.) { return none; }
  let lp = *f.limPos[k] * (1. - u) + *f.limPos[k + 1usize] * u;
  let ln = *f.limNeg[k] * (1. - u) + *f.limNeg[k + 1usize] * u;
  let ar = slotFoot(depth, slotTab(f, t, 1usize), 1., lp, ln);
  let af = slotFoot(depth, slotTab(f, t, 2usize), -1., lp, ln);
  if !(ar > af) { return none; }
  // Only the surface that lies near the opening's plane is the opening: a place over or under it (another part of
  // the surface, further along the normal than half the opening's width) is not folded
  if ((p - h.q).dot(nn)).abs() > 0.5 * (ar - af) { return none; }
  SlotLocal(true, (p - h.q).dot(side), ar, af, depth, nn * (-1.), side)
}

// How far the fold moves the place p: the wall's place for the one the plane had, along the side and along INTO
fn slotOffset(f: &SlotField, p: Vec3) Vec3 {
  let zero = Vec3(0., 0., 0.);
  let l = slotLocal(f, p);
  if !l.ok { return zero; }
  if !(l.a < l.ar && l.a > l.af) { return zero; }
  let u = (l.ar - l.a) / (l.ar - l.af);
  var a2: f32 = 0.;
  var b2: f32 = 0.;
  if u <= 0.5 {
    let g = 2. * u;
    a2 = l.ar * (1. - g);
    b2 = l.depth * g;
  } else {
    let g = 2. * (1. - u);
    a2 = l.af * (1. - g);
    b2 = l.depth * g;
  }
  l.side * (a2 - l.a) + l.down * b2
}

// Whether the place is in the opening (a margin of 1e-4 of it) and not beyond the path's ends
fn slotInBand(f: &SlotField, p: Vec3) bool {
  let l = slotLocal(f, p);
  if !l.ok { return false; }
  let tol = 0.0001 * (l.ar - l.af) + 0.000001;
  l.a >= l.af - tol && l.a <= l.ar + tol
}

fn slotRefused(m: &PolyMesh, problems: &mut List[String], why: &str) PolyMesh {
  var s = String.from("foldSlot: ");
  s.append(why);
  problems.push(s);
  m.clone()
}

pub fn foldSlot(m: &PolyMesh, path: &Path, sections: &List[RunCurve], width: f32, maxEdge: f32, maxPasses: u32,
    problems: &mut List[String]) PolyMesh {
  let np = path.points.len();
  if np < 2usize { return slotRefused(m, problems, "the path has fewer than 2 points"); }
  if !(width > 0.) { return slotRefused(m, problems, "width is not above 0"); }
  if !(maxEdge > 0.) { return slotRefused(m, problems, "maxEdge is not above 0"); }
  if sections.len() != 3usize { return slotRefused(m, problems, "sections are not 3 curves (depth, roof, floor)"); }
  let dist = path.distances();
  let total = *dist[np - 1usize];
  if !(total > 0.) { return slotRefused(m, problems, "the path has no length"); }

  // The sections, sampled: 16 to a path piece (at least 64), linear between samples
  var ts = 16usize * (np - 1usize);
  if ts < 64usize { ts = 64usize; }
  var tab = List[f32].withCapacity(3usize * (ts + 1usize));
  let twoRight: f32 = 3.1415927;
  var footCapped = false;
  var i = 0usize;
  while i <= ts {
    let t = f32.from(i) / f32.from(ts);
    let d = sections[0usize].at(t);
    let roofA = sections[1usize].at(t);
    let floorA = sections[2usize].at(t);
    if !(d >= 0.) { return slotRefused(m, problems, "a depth is below 0 (or not a number)"); }
    if d > 0. {
      if !(roofA > 0.) || !(floorA > 0.) || !(roofA < twoRight) || !(floorA < twoRight) {
        return slotRefused(m, problems, "a wall's angle is not between 0 and two right angles");
      }
      let ar = d * roofA.cos() / roofA.sin();
      let af = -d * floorA.cos() / floorA.sin();
      if af > ar + 0.000001 { return slotRefused(m, problems, "the walls cross at positive depth (the floor's foot is beyond the roof's)"); }
      if ar > width || ar < -width || af > width || af < -width { footCapped = true; }
    }
    tab.push(d);
    tab.push(roofA);
    tab.push(floorA);
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
  if footCapped {
    problems.push(String.from("foldSlot: a wall's foot is farther than width from the path; it is held to width (the wall is steeper)"));
  }

  // The frame at each path point: the tangent, and a first guess of the base normal from the vertices near it
  let vn = m.vertexNormals();
  let nv = m.vertexCount();
  var tan = List[Vec3].withCapacity(np);
  var nrm = List[Vec3].withCapacity(np);
  i = 0usize;
  while i < np {
    let c = *path.points[i];
    let tg = path.tangentAt(i);
    var acc = Vec3(0., 0., 0.);
    var v = 0usize;
    while v < nv {
      let d = *m.positions[v] - c;
      if d.dot(d) <= width * width { acc = acc + *vn[v]; }
      v = v + 1usize;
    }
    var sq = acc - tg * acc.dot(tg);
    if !(sq.dot(sq) > 0.) { return slotRefused(m, problems, "a path point has no surface within width"); }
    if path.up.dot(path.up) > 0. {
      let hint = path.up - tg * path.up.dot(tg);
      if hint.dot(hint) > 0. { sq = hint; }
    }
    tan.push(tg);
    nrm.push(unit(sq));
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
  var lim = SlotField(path.points.clone(), dist, total, tan, nrm, List[f32].withCapacity(np), List[f32].withCapacity(np),
    tab, ts, width);
  i = 0usize;
  while i < np {
    lim.limPos.push(width);
    lim.limNeg.push(width);
    i = i + 1usize;
  }

  // The normal at the opening: the unit normals of the faces whose centres lie near the opening's middle, in two rounds
  var round = 0u32;
  while round < 2u32 {
    i = 0usize;
    while i < np {
      let t = *lim.dist[i] / total;
      let d = slotTab(&lim, t, 0usize);
      if d > 0. {
        let tg = *lim.tan[i];
        let side = unit((*lim.nrm[i]).cross(tg));
        let ar = slotFoot(d, slotTab(&lim, t, 1usize), 1., width, width);
        let af = slotFoot(d, slotTab(&lim, t, 2usize), -1., width, width);
        let mid = *lim.pts[i] + side * ((ar + af) * 0.5);
        let rad = 0.3 * (ar - af) + 0.000001;
        var slab: f32 = 0.;
        if i > 0usize { slab = (*lim.pts[i] - *lim.pts[i - 1usize]).length(); }
        if i + 1usize < np {
          let s2 = (*lim.pts[i + 1usize] - *lim.pts[i]).length();
          if s2 > slab { slab = s2; }
        }
        slab = slab * 0.6;
        var acc = Vec3(0., 0., 0.);
        var f = 0usize;
        while f < m.faceCount() {
          let c = m.faceCentroid(u32.from(f));
          if (c - mid).length() <= rad && (c - *lim.pts[i]).dot(tg).abs() <= slab {
            acc = acc + m.faceNormal(u32.from(f));
          }
          f = f + 1usize;
        }
        let sq = acc - tg * acc.dot(tg);
        if sq.dot(sq) > 0.0001 { lim.nrm.set(i, unit(sq)); }
      }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    round = round + 1u32;
  }

  // The mean edge with an end in the opening
  var sumEdge: f64 = 0.0;
  var nEdge = 0usize;
  var e = 0usize;
  while e < m.edgeCount() {
    let pa = *m.positions[usize.from(m.fromVertex(2u32 * u32.from(e)))];
    let pb = *m.positions[usize.from(m.toVertex(2u32 * u32.from(e)))];
    if slotInBand(&lim, pa) || slotInBand(&lim, pb) {
      sumEdge = sumEdge + f64.from((pa - pb).length());
      nEdge = nEdge + 1usize;
    }
    e = e + 1usize;
  }
  if nEdge == 0usize { return m.clone(); }
  let edge = f32.from(sumEdge / f64.from(nEdge));

  // Bends: the neighbouring planes meet at ds / theta from the path, on the inside
  var bendLo = np;
  var bendHi = 0usize;
  var narrow = width;
  var k = 0usize;
  while k + 1usize < np {
    let t0 = *lim.tan[k];
    let t1 = *lim.tan[k + 1usize];
    let ds = (*lim.pts[k + 1usize] - *lim.pts[k]).length();
    let theta = libc.atan2f(t0.cross(t1).length(), t0.dot(t1));
    if theta > 0.000001 && ds / theta < width {
      let rho = ds / theta;
      let nn = unit(*lim.nrm[k] + *lim.nrm[k + 1usize]);
      let tm = unit(t0 + t1);
      let side = unit(nn.cross(tm));
      let inside = (t1 - t0).dot(side) > 0.;
      var j = k;
      while j <= k + 1usize {
        if inside {
          if rho < *lim.limPos[j] { lim.limPos.set(j, rho); }
        } else {
          if rho < *lim.limNeg[j] { lim.limNeg.set(j, rho); }
        }
        j = j + 1usize;
      }
      if k < bendLo { bendLo = k; }
      if k + 1usize > bendHi { bendHi = k + 1usize; }
      if rho < narrow { narrow = rho; }
    }
    k = k + 1usize;
  }
  if bendHi > 0usize {
    if narrow < edge { return slotRefused(m, problems, "the bend limits the band below one edge of the input"); }
    var s = String.from("foldSlot: the path bends so sharply that neighbouring planes meet within width, at stations ");
    s.appendUInt(u64.from(bendLo));
    s.append(" to ");
    s.appendUInt(u64.from(bendHi));
    s.append("; the band is limited there to ");
    s.appendF32(narrow);
    s.append(" (width ");
    s.appendF32(width);
    s.append(")");
    problems.push(s);
  }

  // The region: the faces with a vertex in the opening
  var inBand = List[bool].withCapacity(nv);
  var v = 0usize;
  while v < nv {
    inBand.push(slotInBand(&lim, *m.positions[v]));
    v = v + 1usize;
  }
  var region = List[u32]();
  var f = 0usize;
  while f < m.faceCount() {
    let vs = m.faceVertices(u32.from(f));
    var hit = false;
    var j = 0usize;
    while j < vs.len() {
      if *inBand[usize.from(*vs[j])] { hit = true; }
      j = j + 1usize;
    }
    if hit { region.push(u32.from(f)); }
    f = f + 1usize;
  }
  if region.len() == 0usize { return m.clone(); }
  var on = DsOnto(false, false, List[Footprint](), List[SurfaceIndex](), List[f32](), 0u32, 0u32, 0u32, List[SlotField]());
  on.slot.push(lim);
  let patch = HeightPatch(Vec3(0., 0., 0.), Vec3(0., 0., 0.), Vec3(0., 0., 0.), Vec3(0., 0., 1.), 0u32, 0u32, List[f32]());
  dsRun(m, region.view(), &patch, &mut on, &List[Vec3](), &List[f32](), maxEdge, maxPasses, problems)
}
